-- erwartet: E001
-- **«B3», paper cut 1 of five.** The first attempt at `add two numbers`, and it is the
-- attempt every reader makes: a function written the way it is written in every other
-- language. `effects` is obligatory and not fail-open, so it falls -- correctly.
--
-- **What this probe holds is the NOTE under the refusal, not the refusal.** The measured
-- session read *"`sum` has no `effects` clause"* and then spent two more attempts guessing
-- the SHAPE of the clause: `effects {}` (`581`) and `effects pure` (`582`). A message that
-- names what is missing without showing what to write costs one attempt per reader.
module gift580 {

pub fn sum(a : u32 in 0 .. 1000, b : u32 in 0 .. 1000) -> u32 in 0 .. 2000
    costs <= 4 ops
{
    return a + b;
}

}
